---
import Layout from "@/layouts/Layout.astro";
import Now from "@/components/Now.astro";
import { level, xp } from "@/data/level";
---

<Layout title="Pavel Kleisner - Independent Senior Backend Engineer & Team Lead">

    <section class="hero">
        <img class="avatar" src="/pavel.jpg" alt="Pavel Kleisner" width="300" height="300" />
        <div>
            <p class="kicker">Senior backend engineer · team lead · <b>level {level}</b></p>
            <h1>Pavel Kleisner</h1>
            <p class="sub">I build and look after the backend systems real businesses run on, and I stay around for what happens after the deploy.</p>
            <div class="actions">
                <a class="btn" href="mailto:contact@pavelkleisner.dev">contact@pavelkleisner.dev</a>
                <a href="/projects">Full quest log</a>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

    <dl class="sheet" aria-label="Character sheet">
        <div><dt>Class</dt><dd>Backend engineer</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Level</dt><dd>{level} years in production</dd><dd class="xp" title={`${xp} % to level ${level + 1}`}><span style={`width:${xp}%`}></span></dd></div>
        <div><dt>Home base</dt><dd>Near Prague, remote</dd></div>
        <div class="lfg"><dt>Party status</dt><dd>Open to contracts</dd></div>
    </dl>

    <div class="book">
        <nav class="toc" aria-label="On this page">
            <p>Character sheet</p>
            <a href="#quests">Quest log</a>
            <a href="#abilities">Abilities</a>
            <a href="#companion">Companion</a>
            <a href="#boss">Boss fight</a>
            <a href="#skills">Skill tree</a>
            <a href="#save">Current save</a>
        </nav>

        <div>
            <section class="chapter" id="quests">
                <h2>Quest log</h2>
                <div class="quests">
                    <article class="quest">
                        <div class="quest-head"><span class="badge b-main">Main quest</span><h3>TSM / CETIN</h3><span class="when">2020 – now</span></div>
                        <p class="role">Senior backend and integration engineer, team lead</p>
                        <div class="quest-body split">
                            <p>Kotlin and Java services on PostgreSQL for a telco operator's service platform: B2B flows, change management, partner integrations and incident analysis.</p>
                            <ul class="objectives">
                                <li>Lead the 2.2 production rollout</li>
                                <li>Lead the 2.4 production rollout</li>
                                <li>Core developer on version 1.5</li>
                            </ul>
                        </div>
                    </article>
                    <article class="quest">
                        <div class="quest-head"><span class="badge b-side">Side quest</span><h3>Nordic web</h3><span class="when">2024 – now, on demand</span></div>
                        <p class="role">Focused changes in a Django codebase when they're needed.</p>
                    </article>
                    <article class="quest past">
                        <div class="quest-head"><span class="badge b-done">Completed</span><h3>MNCP</h3><span class="when">2018 – 2021</span></div>
                        <p class="role">Full-stack Kotlin/Spring and Angular: authentication, exports, archives, measurement batches.</p>
                    </article>
                    <article class="quest past">
                        <div class="quest-head"><span class="badge b-done">Completed</span><h3>ZIS</h3><span class="when">2017 – 2018</span></div>
                        <p class="role">Enterprise Java and ZK. Where I learned to deliver a feature end to end.</p>
                    </article>
                </div>
            </section>

            <section class="chapter" id="abilities">
                <h2>Abilities</h2>
                <dl class="rows">
                    <div><dt>Integrations</dt><dd>B2B APIs, message contracts, retries and the failure modes that only show up once a partner system is connected.</dd></div>
                    <div><dt>Releases</dt><dd>New platform versions into real environments: old data, backward compatibility, rollout order and a way back.</dd></div>
                    <div><dt>Debugging production</dt><dd>Logs, metrics, the database and domain knowledge together. I look for the cause, not for a patch that makes the symptom go quiet.</dd></div>
                    <div><dt>Architecture</dt><dd>Small safe changes, clearly named rules and sensible service boundaries. As little ceremony as the problem allows.</dd></div>
                </dl>
            </section>

            <section class="chapter" id="companion">
                <h2><span class="badge b-party">Companion</span> AI in the party</h2>
                <ul>
                    <li>I use AI agents every day and I've learned to get a lot out of them: exploring an unfamiliar codebase, drafting the boring parts, running tests, preparing migrations and reviewing a diff before I do.</li>
                    <li>It makes me noticeably faster and lets me take on work I wouldn't have had time for.</li>
                    <li>It doesn't take the controller. I read and understand every line that ships under my name, and when production breaks, the analysis and the fix are mine.</li>
                </ul>
            </section>

            <section class="chapter" id="boss">
                <h2><span class="badge b-boss">Boss fight</span> The UUID that wasn't a UUID</h2>
                <p>When we rolled out the first platform version, the integration spec said the <code>messageId</code> would be a UUID. One partner started failing straight away: their system had been quietly parsing the ticket ID out of the old <code>ticketId_timestamp</code> format, even though the ticket ID sat right there in the message body.</p>
                <p>The clean fix was on their side, but in a corporate setting it would have taken months. So I switched our side back to the old shape and production kept running. Sometimes the right call isn't the pure one. It's the one that doesn't break someone else at 2 a.m.</p>
            </section>

            <section class="chapter" id="skills">
                <h2>Skill tree</h2>
                <dl class="skills">
                    <div><dt>Main</dt><dd>Kotlin, Java, Spring, PostgreSQL, Kafka</dd></div>
                    <div><dt>Also unlocked</dt><dd>Kubernetes, Oracle, Angular, Python and Django, TypeScript, Astro</dd></div>
                </dl>
            </section>

            <section class="chapter" id="save">
                <h2>Current save</h2>
                <Now lang="en" />
            </section>
        </div>
    </div>

    <section class="party">
        <div>
            <h2>Looking for a party member?</h2>
            <p>Long-term or focused contracts on backend systems, integrations and production releases.</p>
        </div>
        <a href="mailto:contact@pavelkleisner.dev">contact@pavelkleisner.dev</a>
    </section>

</Layout>
